---
// Field-oriented control block diagram.
---
<svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 720 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="fl-title fl-desc">
  <title id="fl-title">Block diagram of field-oriented control</title>
  <desc id="fl-desc">Two phase currents are measured and converted by the Clarke and Park transforms into d and q components in the rotor's frame. Two PI controllers compare them with their references: i-q reference from the torque command, i-d reference usually zero. Their voltage outputs are rotated back by the inverse Park transform, turned into switch timings by space-vector modulation, and applied by the inverter. The rotor angle from the encoder feeds both rotations.</desc>
  <defs><marker id="ah-fl" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" class="arrowhead" /></marker></defs>
  <!-- forward path q -->
  <text x="10" y="46" class="t-small t-strong">torque command</text><text x="24" y="62" class="t-small t-math">i_q*</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="52" y1="66" x2="86" y2="66" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <circle class="surface wire" cx="99" cy="66" r="12" /><text x="99" y="71" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">−</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="111" y1="66" x2="134" y2="66" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <rect class="soft4 c4" stroke-width="1.4" x="136" y="46" width="56" height="40" rx="7" /><text x="164" y="71" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">PI</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="192" y1="66" x2="246" y2="66" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" /><text x="218" y="58" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small t-math">v_q</text>
  <!-- forward path d -->
  <text x="10" y="118" class="t-small t-math">i_d* = 0</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="52" y1="130" x2="86" y2="130" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <circle class="surface wire" cx="99" cy="130" r="12" /><text x="99" y="135" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">−</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="111" y1="130" x2="134" y2="130" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <rect class="soft4 c4" stroke-width="1.4" x="136" y="110" width="56" height="40" rx="7" /><text x="164" y="135" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">PI</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="192" y1="130" x2="246" y2="130" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" /><text x="218" y="122" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small t-math">v_d</text>
  <!-- inverse park -->
  <rect class="soft1 c1" stroke-width="1.4" x="248" y="46" width="92" height="104" rx="8" />
  <text x="294" y="92" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">Inverse</text><text x="294" y="110" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">Park</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="340" y1="98" x2="372" y2="98" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <rect class="soft1 c1" stroke-width="1.4" x="374" y="64" width="92" height="68" rx="8" />
  <text x="420" y="94" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">SVPWM</text><text x="420" y="111" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small t-muted">switch timing</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="466" y1="98" x2="498" y2="98" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <rect class="soft3 c3" stroke-width="1.4" x="500" y="64" width="86" height="68" rx="8" /><text x="543" y="103" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">Inverter</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="586" y1="98" x2="618" y2="98" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <circle class="soft3 c3" stroke-width="1.6" cx="662" cy="98" r="42" /><text x="662" y="103" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">Motor</text>
  <!-- feedback: currents -->
  <path class="wire" d="M604 98 V242 H468" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <circle class="ink-fill" cx="604" cy="98" r="3" />
  <text x="540" y="234" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">phase currents</text>
  <rect class="soft2 c2" stroke-width="1.4" x="374" y="216" width="92" height="52" rx="8" /><text x="420" y="247" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">Clarke</text>
  <line class="wire" x1="374" y1="242" x2="342" y2="242" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <rect class="soft2 c2" stroke-width="1.4" x="248" y="216" width="92" height="52" rx="8" /><text x="294" y="247" text-anchor="middle" class="t-strong">Park</text>
  <path class="wire" d="M248 232 H99 V144" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" /><text x="176" y="226" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small t-math">i_d</text>
  <path class="wire" d="M248 254 H70 V92 L90 75" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" /><text x="176" y="272" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small t-math">i_q</text>
  <!-- angle -->
  <path class="wire-muted dash" d="M662 140 V300 H294 V270" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <path class="wire-muted dash" d="M294 216 V152" marker-end="url(#ah-fl)" />
  <text x="478" y="316" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small">rotor angle θ from the encoder</text>
  <text x="360" y="22" text-anchor="middle" class="t-small t-muted">Everything left of the Park blocks works on steady (DC) quantities — which is why simple PI controllers suffice.</text>
</svg>
